; Leg HA -- THE REGRESSION LEG.  Host SENDS; the Victor receives.
;
; BENCH take-file: there is no "set line" here.  ~/.kermrc names the adapter.
; CHECK THAT IT NAMES THE ONE THAT IS PLUGGED IN.
;
; CONTROL: SS16aq legs KA/KC/KN_2, three legs with a 16 ms spread --
;     25.652 / 25.659 / 25.668 s, 1,277 cps, 37,557 wire bytes,
;     18 packets, 0 timeouts, 0 resends, rxpeak 409-488.
; The Victor's binary has not been at 38400 since SS16au: since then it took
; upstream 11.0.508, edits 19-22 and SS16av's six fixes, all measured at 9600
; under MAME only.  SS16w says code size is execution time on this machine and
; ~950 bytes moved, so a floor that has SHIFTED is what this leg can see.
;
; START THE VICTOR FIRST.  It takes about 40 s to load; wait for the drive
; to go quiet, then start this.
;
; Check "bulk sel=1" on the .OUT BEFORE reading the clock -- an equivalence
; test cannot see a switch that silently failed (SS16aq).
;
; READ IT WITH:
;     python3 v9k/tools/pktstat.py --rxbytes <from STEPHA.OUT> s16bcHA.pkt
; Residual -11 clean, +28 with a startup timeout.
; cmp FIRST, then the counters.  A leg that is fast and wrong is the failure.

set speed 38400
set receive timeout 20
set parity none
set prefixing cautious
set block 3
set retry 30
log packets s16bcHP.pkt
send rcvhp.dat
statistics
